WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.815 --> 00:00:05.690
<i>Two gunmen have been shot dead</i>

2
00:00:05.773 --> 00:00:08.001
<i>after they opened fire
in a shopping center...</i>

3
00:00:08.091 --> 00:00:10.000
<i>As many as 80, 000 residents of the city</i>

4
00:00:10.089 --> 00:00:12.078
<i>have fled their homes
to escape the shooting...</i>

5
00:00:12.167 --> 00:00:14.042
<i>Government forces
in the southern Philippines</i>

6
00:00:14.125 --> 00:00:15.920
<i>have launched
an offensive against rebels</i>

7
00:00:16.003 --> 00:00:17.753
<i>as fighting escalates
in this part</i>

8
00:00:17.841 --> 00:00:19.591
<i>of Asia's largest
Catholic country.</i>

9
00:00:19.679 --> 00:00:22.271
<i>A national day of mourning
in the Philippines</i>

10
00:00:22.357 --> 00:00:26.346
<i>after 44 police commandos
were killed in the line of duty</i>

11
00:00:26.433 --> 00:00:28.422
<i>when an anti-terror
operation went wrong.</i>

12
00:00:28.511 --> 00:00:30.340
<i>Two hundred
heavily armed separatists</i>

13
00:00:30.429 --> 00:00:32.224
<i>from the National
Liberation Front</i>

14
00:00:32.307 --> 00:00:33.341
<i>attacked the city of Zamboanga.</i>

15
00:00:33.466 --> 00:00:36.503
<i>The officers from the
police special action force were killed</i>

16
00:00:36.543 --> 00:00:41.009
<i>during an operation to capture one
of the most wanted terrorists.</i>

17
00:01:06.273 --> 00:01:09.421
<i>Philippine authorities now
say the toll in yesterday's hotel bombing</i>

18
00:01:09.510 --> 00:01:13.135
<i>has risen to 146 dead
and 231 wounded.</i>

19
00:01:13.226 --> 00:01:17.737
<i>It is the most devastating terrorist
attack in Asia in 10 years</i>

20
00:01:17.821 --> 00:01:19.775
<i>and the worst ever in Manila.</i>

21
00:01:20.259 --> 00:01:23.691
<i>While no organization has taken
responsibility for the blast,</i>

22
00:01:23.775 --> 00:01:27.447
<i>Western intelligence sources
have identified chemical traces</i>

23
00:01:27.531 --> 00:01:32.396
<i>that are the hallmark of the
infamous arms dealer, Aamir Barkawi.</i>

24
00:01:34.165 --> 00:01:36.119
<i>International
security experts say</i>

25
00:01:36.243 --> 00:01:40.391
<i>the Barkawi family is now instigating
violence in remote capitals</i>

26
00:01:40.518 --> 00:01:43.791
<i>to foster instability
and thus fuel</i>

27
00:01:43.875 --> 00:01:47.182
<i>massive arms sales
around the globe.</i>

28
00:02:21.797 --> 00:02:22.865
There he is.

29
00:02:22.956 --> 00:02:24.751
Kamran.
Raza.

30
00:02:26.592 --> 00:02:28.706
Did Philippine
intelligence track you?

31
00:02:30.548 --> 00:02:31.775
Okay.

32
00:02:32.906 --> 00:02:34.054
Father.

33
00:02:36.702 --> 00:02:37.770
Hmm.

34
00:02:42.936 --> 00:02:44.004
You did well.

35
00:02:44.095 --> 00:02:45.094
Thank you.

36
00:02:45.174 --> 00:02:47.639
We need to discuss
Major General Rahman.

37
00:02:48.850 --> 00:02:50.884
It's your
sister's wedding.

38
00:02:51.487 --> 00:02:53.555
I'm sorry.
This can't wait.

39
00:02:56.842 --> 00:02:59.512
I think your ISI officer
was compromised.

40
00:02:59.599 --> 00:03:04.509
Kamran, all Pakistani intelligence
officers are compromised.

41
00:03:04.914 --> 00:03:06.789
One of our Afghani
friends discovered

42
00:03:06.912 --> 00:03:08.866
a German BND agent
in his circle.

43
00:03:08.950 --> 00:03:10.018
And?

44
00:03:14.864 --> 00:03:18.058
That particular general won't
be very useful to us anymore.

45
00:03:18.141 --> 00:03:19.618
He's been eliminated.

46
00:03:22.856 --> 00:03:24.606
Thought you might
want to know.

47
00:03:24.694 --> 00:03:26.285
Don't forget
his family.

48
00:03:27.691 --> 00:03:29.884
Vengeance
must always be

49
00:03:29.969 --> 00:03:32.037
profound and absolute.

50
00:03:37.042 --> 00:03:40.270
So am I.
I'm very happy.

51
00:04:50.768 --> 00:04:54.280
Pentagon just received target
confirmation from MI6 ground asset.

52
00:04:54.364 --> 00:04:55.796
You're clear
to execute.

53
00:05:36.642 --> 00:05:38.631
Hell of a
presidential race, sir.

54
00:05:40.558 --> 00:05:42.274
Every day
the same damn joke.

55
00:05:47.831 --> 00:05:49.024
Seriously?

56
00:05:50.348 --> 00:05:51.575
What the hell did
they make you out of?

57
00:05:51.667 --> 00:05:53.496
Bourbon and poor choices.

58
00:05:56.822 --> 00:05:58.458
You pick a name yet?

59
00:05:59.699 --> 00:06:01.892
We were thinking Benjamin
if it was a boy.

60
00:06:01.977 --> 00:06:03.091
Really?

61
00:06:03.176 --> 00:06:04.243
Hell no!

62
00:06:06.213 --> 00:06:07.849
If it's a girl, maybe.

63
00:06:14.524 --> 00:06:15.592
Voight,

64
00:06:17.281 --> 00:06:18.633
you wanna
run over him for me?

65
00:06:19.160 --> 00:06:21.227
Believe me, sir,
we've tried.

66
00:06:28.031 --> 00:06:29.303
Baby?

67
00:06:31.587 --> 00:06:32.939
Babe.

68
00:06:39.619 --> 00:06:40.618
Mmm.

69
00:06:45.773 --> 00:06:46.772
What?

70
00:06:48.610 --> 00:06:50.360
Little problem
in the nursery.

71
00:06:50.448 --> 00:06:53.278
All right,
so six cameras, right?

72
00:06:53.365 --> 00:06:55.923
One, two, three,

73
00:06:56.003 --> 00:06:58.833
four, five, six.

74
00:06:58.920 --> 00:07:00.909
What, is that too much?
Yeah, maybe.

75
00:07:00.998 --> 00:07:03.225
Yeah, it's too much.
I thought that.

76
00:07:03.315 --> 00:07:04.827
They're baby gifts
from the guys.

77
00:07:06.472 --> 00:07:07.620
I'll take them down.

78
00:07:07.711 --> 00:07:11.586
All we need
is one baby monitor.

79
00:07:11.667 --> 00:07:13.860
One baby monitor,
right, okay.

80
00:07:14.584 --> 00:07:17.857
And a Kevlar mattress.

81
00:07:20.099 --> 00:07:21.246
Come here.

82
00:07:24.614 --> 00:07:26.603
Unhand me.
Never.

83
00:07:26.692 --> 00:07:29.203
And guess who just got
the next week off?

84
00:07:29.289 --> 00:07:31.967
Oh, don't toy with me, young man,
'cause there will be consequences.

85
00:07:32.007 --> 00:07:33.961
No, no, we're finishing
this nursery.

86
00:07:34.045 --> 00:07:36.192
I can't believe it's
taken me this long.

87
00:07:37.761 --> 00:07:39.715
Paint samples.
What?

88
00:07:39.799 --> 00:07:44.151
Yeah. Oh, I gotta show you these
amazing new paint samples.

89
00:07:44.234 --> 00:07:45.268
Can I get
a shower first?

90
00:07:45.353 --> 00:07:46.352
God, yes!

91
00:08:43.535 --> 00:08:45.808
Sir, Speaker of the House
is waiting.

92
00:08:45.893 --> 00:08:48.802
And the Senate Majority Leader
would like five of your time.

93
00:08:48.890 --> 00:08:50.446
Oh. Um...

94
00:08:50.848 --> 00:08:52.359
I'll take him first.
Hmm.

95
00:08:54.124 --> 00:08:55.397
When is Trumbull
getting back?

96
00:08:55.483 --> 00:08:57.790
The Vice President has three
more days of vacation

97
00:08:57.881 --> 00:08:59.471
and insinuated
considerable violence

98
00:08:59.599 --> 00:09:01.155
if he heard my voice before then.

99
00:09:01.237 --> 00:09:04.271
Yeah, never get between
that man and a fish.

100
00:09:04.354 --> 00:09:06.422
Sir, I got your son
on video chat.

101
00:09:06.512 --> 00:09:07.785
Excellent.

102
00:09:08.150 --> 00:09:09.343
He had his first date
last night.

103
00:09:09.429 --> 00:09:12.338
Mr. President,
you need to take this, sir.

104
00:09:12.426 --> 00:09:13.938
Sir,
Speaker of the House?

105
00:09:14.784 --> 00:09:16.420
You need to
take this now, sir.

106
00:09:22.376 --> 00:09:23.728
This is the President.

107
00:09:34.764 --> 00:09:37.195
Okay. Thank you.

108
00:09:41.677 --> 00:09:43.108
<i>Sources confirmed</i>

109
00:09:43.195 --> 00:09:45.502
<i>that Prime Minister
James Wilson has died</i>

110
00:09:45.593 --> 00:09:48.548
<i>while sleeping in his residence
at 10 Downing Street.</i>

111
00:09:48.670 --> 00:09:50.624
<i>He is believed to have
suffered a heart attack,</i>

112
00:09:50.708 --> 00:09:54.094
<i>possibly from complications
after a surgical procedure</i>

113
00:09:54.184 --> 00:09:56.332
<i>to repair his knee
a day earlier.</i>

114
00:09:56.422 --> 00:09:59.252
<i>An autopsy has been scheduled
within the next 48 hours</i>

115
00:09:59.339 --> 00:10:01.134
<i>to determine
the actual cause of death.</i>

116
00:10:01.217 --> 00:10:02.216
It's the White House.

117
00:10:06.772 --> 00:10:09.567
It's okay.
My mom can come over.

118
00:10:27.511 --> 00:10:28.590
What we are proposing

119
00:10:29.349 --> 00:10:32.543
is that the funeral takes
place this Thursday, the 9th,

120
00:10:32.626 --> 00:10:34.376
4:00 p.m.
at St. Paul's.

121
00:10:34.584 --> 00:10:37.493
The confirmed attendees
are all world leaders,

122
00:10:37.581 --> 00:10:40.138
with the lone exception
of the Russian president.

123
00:10:40.218 --> 00:10:41.809
Well,
no love lost there.

124
00:10:41.976 --> 00:10:45.170
Our Royal Family will
attend a private service

125
00:10:45.253 --> 00:10:47.082
at St. James's Palace,
the morning of,

126
00:10:47.171 --> 00:10:51.080
with 28 other heads of state
from all over the globe.

127
00:10:51.167 --> 00:10:54.759
As per foreign royals,
Prince Albert of Monaco,

128
00:10:54.844 --> 00:10:57.230
Queen Rania of Jordan,
Saudi Prince Muqrin.

129
00:10:57.321 --> 00:10:59.310
Yes, it's a
logistical nightmare.

130
00:11:00.278 --> 00:11:03.187
But let's make sure
this runs without a hitch.

131
00:11:03.435 --> 00:11:04.549
Questions?

132
00:11:05.513 --> 00:11:09.343
And what special requests have
the Yank circus demanded so far?

133
00:11:09.469 --> 00:11:12.424
Dallas Cowboy cheerleaders
part of the retinue, possibly?

134
00:11:12.506 --> 00:11:14.779
That's a
request I could live with.

135
00:11:14.864 --> 00:11:19.250
I'm partial to the Kardashians myself,
as apparently is Her Majesty.

136
00:11:20.578 --> 00:11:23.373
Nineteen special requests
from 12 different countries.

137
00:11:23.495 --> 00:11:25.484
We've denied all of them.

138
00:11:26.332 --> 00:11:30.367
Any issues of special concern
with our current assessments?

139
00:11:30.448 --> 00:11:33.005
We all know about the 350
or so British nationals

140
00:11:33.165 --> 00:11:35.403
who've traveled back and forth
to Syria in the past year,

141
00:11:36.202 --> 00:11:39.032
as we've seen before
in Iraq and Afghanistan.

142
00:11:40.278 --> 00:11:42.744
Of rising concern
is the handful

143
00:11:42.836 --> 00:11:44.187
we believe to be
former military.

144
00:11:44.274 --> 00:11:45.592
Is any of this
actionable?

145
00:11:45.673 --> 00:11:47.229
No.

146
00:11:47.351 --> 00:11:48.544
Very well.

147
00:11:49.509 --> 00:11:52.862
Then we will see off our dear
friend James with dignity.

148
00:11:54.504 --> 00:11:56.618
Give him the ceremony
he deserves.

149
00:12:01.936 --> 00:12:03.334
Sir?

150
00:12:03.375 --> 00:12:04.693
Are you ready for us?
Oh.

151
00:12:04.774 --> 00:12:06.091
Yeah, come on in.

152
00:12:07.211 --> 00:12:08.404
Take a seat.

153
00:12:16.282 --> 00:12:18.316
What are you guys
so damn nervous about?

154
00:12:18.760 --> 00:12:21.476
The Brits are world class.
We all know their reputation.

155
00:12:21.557 --> 00:12:24.148
But still, these are
the trips I hate.

156
00:12:24.314 --> 00:12:27.587
Last minute. Out of the country.
No time to plan.

157
00:12:27.671 --> 00:12:29.785
Are you sure I can't
talk you out of this?

158
00:12:30.668 --> 00:12:33.179
Lynne,
it's a state funeral.

159
00:12:33.265 --> 00:12:35.254
It's our oldest,
strongest ally.

160
00:12:35.343 --> 00:12:38.491
I spent half the night on the
line with our advance team.

161
00:12:38.620 --> 00:12:41.689
Metropolitan Police will secure
the perimeter of the funeral

162
00:12:41.777 --> 00:12:42.890
at St. Paul's Cathedral.

163
00:12:43.015 --> 00:12:45.368
Air Force One will land
at Stansted Airport.

164
00:12:45.493 --> 00:12:47.083
On the ground
it's all Mike.

165
00:12:47.171 --> 00:12:52.320
Touchdown. Then a 12-minute
chopper ride to Somerset House.

166
00:12:52.406 --> 00:12:54.793
From there we take
an armored-vehicle escort

167
00:12:54.883 --> 00:12:58.236
down Fleet Street
to the cathedral.

168
00:13:00.158 --> 00:13:01.510
You don't
seem thrilled.

169
00:13:01.637 --> 00:13:03.512
Well, the British
have their hands full.

170
00:13:03.595 --> 00:13:06.789
It's a clusterfuck...
Sir.

171
00:13:06.911 --> 00:13:09.945
Well, 40
different countries

172
00:13:10.028 --> 00:13:11.699
with 40 different
security teams.

173
00:13:12.306 --> 00:13:14.374
Minimal flexibility
on approach routes,

174
00:13:14.464 --> 00:13:16.850
funeral seating, egress.

175
00:13:18.260 --> 00:13:19.328
Can we make it work?

176
00:13:19.419 --> 00:13:20.487
Mike?

177
00:13:21.657 --> 00:13:22.883
I always do, sir.

178
00:13:24.214 --> 00:13:25.213
Good.

179
00:13:25.293 --> 00:13:27.725
I know it's not great
timing for you, but...

180
00:13:29.409 --> 00:13:30.806
It's what I do.

181
00:13:30.887 --> 00:13:32.205
Thank you, sir.

182
00:13:47.351 --> 00:13:48.465
There's my man.

183
00:13:48.550 --> 00:13:51.777
Mr. Vice President.
How was your vacation, sir?

184
00:13:51.946 --> 00:13:56.776
Son, do you have any idea
the joy a man feels

185
00:13:56.861 --> 00:13:58.657
pulling
a 70-pound king mackerel

186
00:13:58.740 --> 00:14:00.456
out of the waters
around Jekyll Island?

187
00:14:00.578 --> 00:14:01.850
No, sir, I don't.

188
00:14:01.936 --> 00:14:03.163
That makes two of us.

189
00:14:03.255 --> 00:14:05.653
And I'll have to wait
until next year to find out.

190
00:14:06.052 --> 00:14:08.280
But thanks for asking.

191
00:14:19.519 --> 00:14:21.269
Oh, yeah,
that's in the Sinai.

192
00:14:21.357 --> 00:14:24.391
- It's beautiful.
- There you go.

193
00:14:24.514 --> 00:14:27.031
Oh, gee, that's incredible.
I love these things. They all are...

194
00:14:30.907 --> 00:14:33.294
Don't worry about a thing.
We'll be fine.

195
00:14:35.742 --> 00:14:37.140
Doris,
can we have a minute?

196
00:14:37.261 --> 00:14:38.693
Sure.

197
00:14:41.257 --> 00:14:42.689
Oh, you meant Leah.
Right.

198
00:14:42.775 --> 00:14:43.889
Very funny, Doris.

199
00:14:46.811 --> 00:14:49.039
And she tells me
not to worry.

200
00:14:50.408 --> 00:14:51.839
It's only three days.

201
00:14:52.566 --> 00:14:54.838
Yeah. And I'm not
due for two weeks.

202
00:14:57.401 --> 00:15:01.231
The walking away ain't
quite so easy this time.

203
00:15:01.357 --> 00:15:05.187
Hey, I got this.

204
00:15:05.273 --> 00:15:07.501
You go and you do
what you have to do

205
00:15:07.631 --> 00:15:12.336
and we will be right here
when you get back, okay?

206
00:15:12.426 --> 00:15:15.415
You, say bye-bye
to Daddy.

207
00:15:16.142 --> 00:15:17.141
Hmm.

208
00:15:17.501 --> 00:15:19.251
Bye-bye, Daddy.

209
00:15:21.297 --> 00:15:23.525
Bell tolls.

210
00:15:23.655 --> 00:15:24.654
Yeah.

211
00:15:29.848 --> 00:15:31.677
I love you.

212
00:15:33.844 --> 00:15:35.595
You better.

213
00:15:36.841 --> 00:15:38.398
Behave.

214
00:16:00.977 --> 00:16:03.284
Uh, here you go.
Thank you.

215
00:16:05.533 --> 00:16:08.646
You've been hiding lately.
You busy nesting?

216
00:16:08.729 --> 00:16:10.797
Something like that.
Mmm-hmm.

217
00:16:10.887 --> 00:16:14.593
Your idea of nesting being bullet-proofing
the walls of the nursery?

218
00:16:14.723 --> 00:16:16.996
Now, that is actually a great idea.

219
00:16:21.517 --> 00:16:22.834
Yes.

220
00:16:25.273 --> 00:16:26.750
I'll do it.

221
00:16:28.869 --> 00:16:32.256
Well...
That only took two weeks.

222
00:16:32.506 --> 00:16:36.017
Uh-uh. It's no small
thing being a godmother.

223
00:16:36.102 --> 00:16:38.693
I mean, I didn't take
your asking lightly.

224
00:16:40.338 --> 00:16:41.406
Oh, I know.

225
00:16:41.497 --> 00:16:43.531
You think
you can handle it?

226
00:16:44.693 --> 00:16:45.932
Well, I'm competent, brilliant,

227
00:16:46.012 --> 00:16:48.444
stunningly beautiful and
really fucking honored.

228
00:16:51.007 --> 00:16:52.325
Really honored.

229
00:16:53.365 --> 00:16:54.364
Thank you, Lynne.

230
00:17:12.426 --> 00:17:13.618
Big day ahead.

231
00:17:13.744 --> 00:17:15.176
Correction. Mega day.

232
00:17:15.463 --> 00:17:16.814
Morning.

233
00:17:18.100 --> 00:17:19.134
Thank you.

234
00:17:22.336 --> 00:17:24.801
Just your signature here, please.
Thank you, sir.

235
00:17:29.529 --> 00:17:30.846
Gentlemen, ladies.

236
00:17:32.006 --> 00:17:34.597
Today, I need
your undivided best.

237
00:17:34.683 --> 00:17:37.877
The most important people in
the world are in our care,

238
00:17:37.960 --> 00:17:40.835
so muck in
and get it right.

239
00:17:40.917 --> 00:17:42.516
Always, Chief. Hmm.

240
00:17:46.112 --> 00:17:48.499
Good morning, London.

241
00:18:02.695 --> 00:18:04.524
Southpaw
has landed.

242
00:18:14.084 --> 00:18:16.437
Agent Banning.
John Lancaster from 5.

243
00:18:16.521 --> 00:18:18.192
Hey, John.
Bit early, aren't you?

244
00:18:18.280 --> 00:18:20.348
Nope.
We're moving up our schedule.

245
00:18:20.478 --> 00:18:21.704
I see.

246
00:18:21.836 --> 00:18:24.825
The fewer people know the President's
exact movements, the better.

247
00:18:24.913 --> 00:18:26.311
Why wasn't I told?

248
00:18:26.392 --> 00:18:27.709
Nobody was.

249
00:18:27.790 --> 00:18:29.506
That's how
you keep it a surprise.

250
00:18:30.348 --> 00:18:31.779
Well,
thanks for the help.

251
00:18:39.179 --> 00:18:41.213
<i>With security at unprecedented levels</i>

252
00:18:41.297 --> 00:18:43.251
<i>in anticipation
of the funeral,</i>

253
00:18:43.335 --> 00:18:45.971
<i>set to begin just
an hour from now,</i>

254
